# AGENTS.md – workspace router

> Codex and agent-compatible tools read this file before the first task. Keep the router concise. Put repeatable procedures in `.agents/skills/` and working data in the folders below.

## Operator

- Role: {one sentence}
- Main language: {Russian / English}
- Primary timezone: {Europe/Lisbon}
- Current process: {one repeatable process}
- Desired result: {one observable output}

## Communication

- Start with the main point.
- Keep answers concise and concrete.
- Use en dash (–), U+2013.
- Surface assumptions and blockers.

## File naming

- New working files: `{project} {type} description – YYYY-MM-DD.ext`.
- Description: latin, lower case, 2–6 words.
- Date: at the end. Separator: en dash (–).
- Allowed types: brief, meeting, research, analysis, process, context, decision, output, log, draft, rule, template, skill, handoff, registry, dataset.
- Runtime files keep fixed names: `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `SKILL.md`.
- The agent checks existing siblings before creating a file.

## Workspace map

- `sources/` – approved inputs for the current process.
- `output/` – observable results of each run.
- `evidence-log.md` – one line per run: result, gap, system update.
- `.agents/skills/` – repeatable procedures.
- `private/` – local-only material. Never include it in public or team output.

## Definition of done

{A measurable quality contract. Example: “The lead reads the status in two minutes; every factual claim links to a source; the result fits one page.”}

## Autonomy boundaries

- `public` – sanitized and publishable; agent may prepare and update local files.
- `team` – internal working material; agent may prepare, operator reviews distribution.
- `local` – stays on this device.
- `external` – sanctioned partner or service source with explicit purpose and owner.
- `ask first` – sending to people, publishing, deleting, spending money, changing permissions.
- `deny` – secrets, unsafe writes and silent outbound actions.

## Continuity

At the end of a meaningful run, update `evidence-log.md` with:

```text
date · result · evidence · gap · next system change
```

The next session starts from the latest output and evidence line.
